There are \(90\) two-digit numbers total, from \(10\) to \(99\).

Half of them are odd and half are even:
- Odd two-digit numbers: \(45\)
- Even two-digit numbers: \(45\)

The product is even unless both chosen numbers are odd. So use the complement:

\[
P(\text{product odd}) = P(\text{both numbers odd})
= \frac{\binom{45}{2}}{\binom{90}{2}}
\]

\[
= \frac{\frac{45\cdot 44}{2}}{\frac{90\cdot 89}{2}}
= \frac{45\cdot 44}{90\cdot 89}
= \frac{22}{89}
\]

Therefore,

\[
P(\text{product even}) = 1 - \frac{22}{89}
= \frac{67}{89}
\]

The answer is \(\boxed{\frac{67}{89}}\).
